WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.090
- I am so excited to have the chance

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:05.290
to share my passion for design
and decorating with you.

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:06.123
In another life,

00:00:06.123 --> 00:00:08.540
I would have been a full
on interior designer.

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:10.930
I'm obsessed with creating fun new spaces

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:13.480
and redecorating my home, friends' homes,

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.340
and now maybe some of your homes,

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:16.690
if I could be so lucky?

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:19.123
This is our first ever Designed by Drew.

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:20.843
Okay.

00:00:20.843 --> 00:00:22.870
Essential workers have become the backbone

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:24.350
of the country this year,

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:27.240
and we have so much to thank them for.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.780
One family right here in our
backyard has been selfless

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:35.320
during this time as all five
members have been going to work

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:36.780
every single day.

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:38.833
Please meet the Copenings.

00:00:39.879 --> 00:00:41.850
(upbeat music)

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:44.830
- Don't let this, you know, us
sitting down here, fool you.

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:46.620
We are a crazy bunch.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:49.560
We are just electric at times, you know.

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:52.220
Everybody's a little
spicy in their own way,

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:54.110
and we just love to have a good time.

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:55.460
You know, you never know what to expect

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:57.170
in the Copening house.

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:01.740
- My name is Michael Copening,
AKA Chocolate Thunder, baby!

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:05.360
- I'm Lachelle, Mama Bear, AKA Chelley!

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:08.110
- Michael Copening Jr., AKA Mike Mike,

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:09.830
so good you gotta say it twice.

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:10.880
- Shakiyah Copening,

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:13.776
I am the middle child
and the favorite child.

00:01:13.776 --> 00:01:15.450
(family laughing)

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:18.696
- And I'm Jay, AKA Jay Smooth, the baby.

00:01:18.696 --> 00:01:21.696
- [Family] And we are the Copenings!

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:23.515
(uplifting music)

00:01:23.515 --> 00:01:27.010
- Me, my husband, my children,
we're all essential workers.

00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:29.740
I am a United States postal clerk.

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:31.210
- I knew I was a front line worker

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:32.590
when I looked at all my neighbors

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:36.720
and they wasn't going to work
in the morning. (laughing)

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:39.130
But I knew somebody got
to take care of the sick.

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:40.960
So if I don't do my job,

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:42.760
then somebody else can't do their job.

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:43.960
Mike Mike was like me,

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:46.250
a directional transportation technician.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:48.950
You may not know what it is,
but it's the bus operator.

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:50.100
That's my son, y'all.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:53.570
You have my daughter, she's
in the board of education.

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:55.680
She takes care of the kids.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:57.690
Jayquan, he works in a nursing home.

00:01:57.690 --> 00:02:02.270
- I'm grateful that we were
not physically affected

00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:04.370
by the virus.

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:07.720
It really had me so
worried and so concerned.

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:10.050
- At first, I didn't take
the COVID too serious

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:12.860
until I learned that I
lost a close coworker.

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:15.890
It made me just say, this is for real.

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:18.060
- That's one of the things
of being a frontline

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:20.270
essential worker is that, you know,

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:21.680
you're not only worried about the people

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:23.430
that you're in the house
with, but you're worried

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:26.328
about the people that
they're connected to.

00:02:26.328 --> 00:02:27.270
- At my nursing home,

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:29.720
I was close to many
residents who passed away.

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:33.310
It was this one resident
that I really got close to,

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:35.090
probably my best friend there.

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:38.260
He got really sick and all the nurses

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:40.330
and everything thought
it was over for him.

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:42.500
And I prayed for him.

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:44.140
I had my whole family pray for him

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:46.280
and he actually made it through.

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:48.650
- We are a family that
supports one another.

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:51.660
So if one of us is down
and somebody need a prayer,

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:54.560
so we all band together as a family.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:56.270
And we said, we're gonna
pray for that person.

00:02:56.270 --> 00:02:57.630
- During the pandemic,

00:02:57.630 --> 00:03:00.837
I felt it was just more than
just taking people to work.

00:03:00.837 --> 00:03:02.940
It was just who I was taking the work,

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:07.830
bringing in the front line
workers, officers, nurses,

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:09.790
doctors, you know, all the above.

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:12.600
- This summer for Hero Day,

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:16.860
I wore an MTA uniform
because I wanted to celebrate

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:19.290
the fact that my brother
and my dad were out there

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:21.880
every day, driving
essential workers to work

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:24.843
and I wanted to celebrate them
because they were my heroes.

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:28.200
(upbeat music)

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:29.670
- The house that we're in right now

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:31.900
is a very special place to me.

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:33.660
I was born and raised there.

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:36.280
And now I have the
pleasure of raising my kids

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:37.550
in the same house.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:40.060
So we all have the same experiences.

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:44.440
- During this pandemic, we
had to find new safe places

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:46.270
for our family to spend time,

00:03:46.270 --> 00:03:48.583
and the backyard was our place.

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:52.810
We have that karaoke
night, almost all the time

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:54.110
when we in the backyard.

00:03:54.110 --> 00:03:55.690
- We learned a lot of card games.

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:57.680
Everybody was learning how to cook,

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:00.350
and it was kind of like
back to our safe space.

00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:04.410
- The Copenings, we're home
safe and sound from work,

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:07.613
headed to the backyard for a barbecue!

00:04:10.188 --> 00:04:11.990
- The backyard is my kingdom back there.

00:04:11.990 --> 00:04:14.429
I do my grilling back there.

00:04:14.429 --> 00:04:16.530
We're going to call this
Cooking with Chocolate.

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:18.600
I could smoke it, I could bake it,

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:21.780
I could fry it, whatever
you want, you can get it.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:24.290
- We always wanted our backyard renovated

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:26.640
since we spend so much time back here.

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:28.970
We just haven't had the opportunity

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:31.100
because we're always working.

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:32.930
- During the summer seasons,

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:36.740
that's where we go to enjoy
food, music, and just relax.

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:41.110
- We have a lot of fun,
but God has blessed us

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:44.920
to raise three strong, responsible kids

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:47.113
that know the meaning family.

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:52.790
- I love this family!

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:55.740
So while the family was having
a good time at the park,

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:58.220
they had no idea what was
happening at their house.

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:00.740
We sent an entire team
to dig up their lawn,

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:03.150
bring a new appliances,
and new patio furniture.

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:04.350
And the craziest part,

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:06.660
we did all of this in just five hours.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:07.580
Look at this crew!

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:10.300
It actually took weeks to set
up, but execute in five hours.

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:11.840
And I can't wait to see their faces

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:14.492
when we reveal their new backyard to them.

00:05:14.492 --> 00:05:17.075
(upbeat music)

